Players: [Proposer, Responder];
Strategies: Proposer = Offer x ∈ {0,1,…,10} units to Responder; Responder = {Accept, Reject};
Standard Payoffs (if Accept): (Proposer: 10‑x, Responder: x); (if Reject): (0,0);
Fehr‑Schmidt utility for Responder (α=1, β=0.5):
U_R(accept,x) = x – α·max{(10‑x)‑x,0} – β·max{x‑(10‑x),0}
= x – max{10‑2x,0} – 0.5·max{2x‑10,0};
Empirical rejection threshold ≈ 3‑4 units (offers ≤3 are rejected >50 % of the time).

